# Security Rules

## Input Validation

**NEVER trust user input.** Validate everything at the API boundary.

| ✅ DO | ❌ DON'T |
|-------|----------|
| Validate all inputs | Trust request data |
| Sanitize output | Render raw HTML |
| Use parameterized queries | String concatenation for SQL |
| Type-check all values | Assume correct types |

---

## Authentication & Authorization

### Authentication

| ✅ DO | ❌ DON'T |
|-------|----------|
| Hash passwords (bcrypt/argon2) | Store plain text |
| Verify JWT signature | Trust unsigned JWTs |
| Use short JWT expiry + refresh | Long-lived tokens |
| Implement rate limiting | Unlimited attempts |
| Use HTTPS everywhere | HTTP in production |

### Authorization

```typescript
// ❌ BAD - Skip authorization
app.get('/api/admin', (req, res) => {
  res.json({ secret: 'data' });
});

// ✅ GOOD - Check role every route
app.get('/api/admin', requireAuth, requireRole('admin'), (req, res) => {
  res.json({ secret: 'data' });
});
```

---

## Secrets Management

| ✅ DO | ❌ DON'T |
|-------|----------|
| Use environment variables | Hardcode secrets |
| Use secret managers (Vault, AWS Secrets) | Commit .env files |
| Rotate secrets regularly | Use same key forever |
| Validate env vars at startup | Ignore missing config |

